WEBVTT

00:46:59.865 --> 00:47:03.241
Just how angry are they?
How scandalous is it?"

00:47:03.265 --> 00:47:05.345
There's no exploration
of this other stuff.

00:47:05.369 --> 00:47:10.533
So the implication of your view
is that most of media

00:47:10.557 --> 00:47:14.066
is missing the most interesting
conversations out there.

00:47:14.090 --> 00:47:16.141
DB: For sure. That's a zillion times true.

00:47:16.165 --> 00:47:18.775
Like I say, we're over-politicized
and under-moralized

00:47:18.799 --> 00:47:21.203
and under-culturalized,
under-technologized.

00:47:21.227 --> 00:47:24.682
You know, I go to TED periodically
and you get to see Sergey Brin.

00:47:24.706 --> 00:47:28.168
You get to see people who literally
will be known in 300 years.

00:47:28.192 --> 00:47:32.016
When we look back on
certain decades -- 1890s, 1880s --